00:37:52,180 --> 00:37:55,500
Imagine you are integrating a physical quantity over a surface,

762
00:37:56,020 --> 00:37:59,220
say, calculating the electromagnetic flux through a sphere.

763
00:37:59,740 --> 00:38:02,900
The mathematics has to know which way is out and which way is in.

764
00:38:03,660 --> 00:38:09,120
Geometrically and physically, reversing the orientation of the surface changes the sign of the integral.

765
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:13,360
So it's the difference between water flowing into a bathtub, adding volume,

766
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:16,660
versus water flowing out of the drain, subtracting volume.

767
00:38:16,780 --> 00:38:17,160
Exactly.

768
00:38:17,680 --> 00:38:23,680
It is the mathematical expression that distinguishes between flux entering a region and flux exiting a region.

769
00:38:24,060 --> 00:38:24,180
Yeah.

770
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:29,080
In the RSVP framework, when you are tracking that vector field and calculating conserved currents,

